Z||000000||Gold87SE||07-04-2000||12:49 AM||||I have an 87 SE with 140,000 miles on it and it has been puzzling me as of late. It's been going through coolant rather quickly and has been overheating often. We tried taking the thermostat out and it was running at around 100 which is way too low. We took the car to a radiator specialist and he checked out the radiator and said everything was fine and put the thermostat back in. He flushed the radiator and let the car idle a good 20 mins and couldn't get it to overheat. The very next day it overheated on me. My car was running very well when I got it(I took it to 120mph and had no problems)I let it sit for 15 mins with the fan on until it cooled off enough to rush it home(I was only 4 blocks away). I rushed it home and barely made it before it overheated again. When I got home I started it up again and it was running horrible. It usually idles at a steady 1000 rpm but now it was idling at 1500 and there was a bit of gray smoke coming out the exhaust with a really sweet smell. I checked the coolant and it was below the add line so I filled it back up and it was still overheating. I then took the thermostat back out and it still overheated. I called up the AW Golden Pontiac Dealership and made an appoitment to have it looked at. The next day I checked the coolant level again and it was still full so I attempted to drive it there and made it 4 block before it overheated. I let it cool off again and raced it home, it was running horrible. We called AAA and had it towed there. When it got there the guy had me back it off the flatbed and park it. When I parked it, it was suddenly running fine again, idling at a steady 1000 rpms and there was no longer grayish whiteish smoke and it no longer smelled. I just got a call today from AW Golden and they told me they're puzzled because they can't find anything wrong with the car and can't get it to overheat, WTF!? The only observation they made is that the person that had the car before me had it rewired. They still have the car now. Does anybody have any idea what could be wrong with my car?||||reg||1
Z||000001||jlruiz67||07-04-2000||01:14 AM||||It might be the water pump. I had a problem with over heating and it did something similar. Other than that I can't help. Good luck, I'm sure that you will find the awnser here.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold87SE||07-04-2000||01:27 AM||||Yeah, I have a friend that knows a lot about cars and he said it might be that and also I told the radiator specialist the problems I was having and he said that too and he even offered to check it and fix it for free if that was the problem but I turned it down because I thought I blew a head gasket and figured it was too late but now apparently I didn't blow a head gasket(Thank God) so I might take him up on that offer.<P>Oh, by the way, the guy that towed the car away was nice enough to tell me that Fiero's are junk and they're the worst cars ever made. Some people can be so ignorant!||||reg||1
